/-!
# Affineness from a rational fixed point

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Proposition 8.9, p.150, and the rational-action
argument of Proposition 8.25, p.154; Milne (2013), arXiv:1311.6060v2, Proposition 4.1,
last paragraph, referring to Proposition 2.6.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-rational-fixed-point-affineness)

The rational map is represented by a Mathlib partial map on its largest domain.
The fixed-section condition is a morphism identity on every test scheme mapping
into that domain; thus it includes infinitesimal test schemes.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory Limits MonoidalCategory CartesianMonoidalCategory MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A faithful action on a dense open with a rational fixed point makes the group affine.

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Proposition 8.9, p.150, and Proposition 8.25,
p.154; Milne (2013), arXiv:1311.6060v2, Proposition 4.1, final paragraph.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-rational-fixed-point-affineness).

Here `α` represents the rational extension on its largest domain, as required by
`hmax`. The lift in `hextends` says that this domain contains G times Y and that
the restriction is the given regular action. The identity section lifts into the
domain by `hdefined`. For `hfixed`, test schemes mapping into the domain along
(g,P) are precisely test schemes of V, the inverse image of that domain along
the section G times P. Equality for these maps says that its restriction is P.

The faithfulness condition is stated as an equality of morphisms K times Y to Y;
this is equivalent to equality after every commutative k-algebra base change.
The conclusion that the inclusion factors through the identity section says
exactly that this closed subgroup is the identity subgroup.

Proof plan:
1. Apply lem-sfb-rational-fixed-section-jets to this rational action and fixed
   section. The whole section lies in the domain, and inverse pullback gives
   compatible representations on the nonzero finite-dimensional jet algebras,
   with descending closed finite-type kernels K_n. No smoothness of X is needed.
2. The field is Noetherian. By lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-over-noetherian G is
   Noetherian. Choose a finite affine Noetherian cover (pqf-def-locnoeth).
   By lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-affine-cover-criterion the kernels correspond
   to increasing ideals on each chart. Their union is finitely generated by
   def-weil-pbc-noetherian-ring, so the chain stabilizes on each chart; take the
   maximum of the finitely many bounds. Write K for the stable kernel.
3. K acts trivially on every jet, by stabilization and compatibility. On the
   intersection of the domain with K times X, apply
   lem-sfb-constant-family-jet-equality to the action and the second projection.
   They agree on every jet, hence on this intersection and on K times Y.
   Faithfulness implies that K is the identity subgroup, scheme-theoretically.
4. The stabilized representation is injective on every algebra's points.
   A basis identifies its target with GL_d, d at least one
   (def-sc-general-linear-group). By
   lem-sfb-algebraic-group-monomorphism-closed-immersion it is a closed immersion.
   The affine-cover criterion for closed immersions then makes G affine. -/
theorem isAffine_of_rational_fixed_point
    {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    (G X Y : Over (Spec (.of k))) [GrpObj G]
    [Smooth G.hom] [ConnectedSpace G.left] [IsSeparated G.hom]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType G.hom] [QuasiCompact G.hom]
    [IsIntegral X.left] [IsSeparated X.hom]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType X.hom] [QuasiCompact X.hom]
    (j : Y ⟶ X) [IsOpenImmersion j.left] [Nonempty Y.left]
    (hdense : Dense (Set.range j.left)) [ModObj G Y]
    (hfaithful : ∀ (K : Over (Spec (.of k))) [GrpObj K]
      (i : K ⟶ G) [IsClosedSubgroupScheme i],
      (i ⊗ₘ 𝟙 Y) ≫ ModObj.smul (M := G) (X := Y) = snd K Y → i = toUnit K ≫ η[G])
    (α : (G ⊗ X).left.PartialMap X.left)
    (hmax : α.domain = α.toRationalMap.domain)
    (hextends : ∃ t : (G ⊗ Y).left ⟶ α.domain.toScheme,
      t ≫ α.domain.ι = (𝟙 G ⊗ₘ j).left ∧
      t ≫ α.hom = (ModObj.smul (M := G) (X := Y) ≫ j).left)
    (P : 𝟙_ (Over (Spec (.of k))) ⟶ X)
    (hdefined : ∃ p : (𝟙_ (Over (Spec (.of k)))).left ⟶ α.domain.toScheme,
      p ≫ α.domain.ι = (lift η[G] P).left)
    (hfixed : ∀ (T : Over (Spec (.of k))) (g : T ⟶ G)
      (d : T.left ⟶ α.domain.toScheme),
      d ≫ α.domain.ι = (lift g (toUnit T ≫ P)).left →
      d ≫ α.hom = (toUnit T ≫ P).left) :
    IsAffine G.left := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
